<title>USA: Nordic Investment Bank files for $193.1 mln debt.</title>
<headline>Nordic Investment Bank files for $193.1 mln debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nordic Investment Bank filed a shelf registration Friday with the Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $193.1 million in debt securities and warrants to purchase debt securities.</p>
<p>Nordic, which finances investment projects and exports of Denmark, Finland, Iceland, Norway and Sweden, said net proceeds from the sale of the securiteis will be used for general operations, including loans that it may grant.</p>
<p>The Helsinki-based bank said that, when combined with a previous registration, it will have up to $750 million of debt securities and warrants available.</p>
</text>
